  "observations": {
    "cosmic_density": "Both upper panels use short overlapping samples of the v10 Nexus poster’s fine filaments, with quieter violet-blue haze behind the foreground.",
    "dark_voids": "Thin texture leaves dark gaps between branching blue and ember paths. Both slices feather into the README's dark background.",
    "luminous_clusters": "Cyan and ember pulses have a compact core, a soft halo, and a short afterglow tied to successive filaments. Both upper loops retain observable motion at 255 px.",
    "vertical_continuity": "One vertical field supplies the opener and continuation. The cyan and ember paths cross the intro break at corresponding positions.",
    "phone_legibility": "The upper panels fill a 255 px column with heights of 112 and 93 px. The approved v10 footer still reads Explore the projects. Build with me.",
    "fibonacci_structure": "The two new upper panels preserve the 21-frame, 130 ms cadence. The unchanged footer retains 34 frames at 80 ms.",
    "handoff_ontology": "Opening light moves from the banner output through two stitched transitions. The closing panel opens the public projects with the approved invitation.",
    "continuous_motion": "Both cold and warm pulses descend with a brief afterglow in 2.73-second loops. The paired quiet PNGs provide the reduced-motion view.",
    "palette": "V10’s blue and ember materials form the foreground of both scenes. Warmer palette entries preserve orange detail at phone width.",
    "pinned_handoff": "Both upper threads open out before the approved v10 closing invitation. Both footer files are byte-identical to the reviewed release."
